experiment: projprobe
  each trial 2000 ms, first 500 discarded; no learning, no reward
  a random sparse binary projection onto 126 units — the linear part
  of a tract, with no threshold and nothing else driving the target.
  instrument        projprobe   trial seed 0000000001357bc2   100 trials per arm
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

    arm                    at source   d=0.03      d=0.15      d=0.40      shuffled
    object from central    0.780       0.580       0.600       0.540       0.500
    object from vision     0.980       0.980       0.940       0.740       0.500
    word from auditory     1.000       1.000       1.000       0.720       0.400

    arm                    coherence   d=0.15      centred     E-I         flipped     flip-shuf
    object from central    0.060       0.600       0.680       0.740       0.760       0.500
    object from vision     0.065       0.940       0.980       0.980       0.940       1.000
    word from auditory     0.130       1.000       1.000       1.000       1.000       1.000

    'at source' is the same number m3probe prints. Read each row across:
    the drop from source to projected is what a tract of that density costs
    this code, before the target neuron has done anything at all.

    The word row is the control and has to hold up — auditory->vocal is a
    real tract at density 0.15 and vocal reads the word at 0.960. If the word
    falls apart here too, the projection is a bad model of a tract and no
